  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing a sarcastic preference",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the bottom textual material ('i just prefer presidents who weren't captured by putin!') as the implied speaker of the sarcastic statement. The meme uses John McCain's image to visually represent this speaker, creating a projection where the user identifies with or imagines themselves as the person making this politically charged, mocking preference. The text directly addresses the user's perspective by framing the statement as a personal, subjective choice, thereby projecting the user's identity onto the textual content.",
